{"raw": {"https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/administrative-assistant-associate-nmsu-satellite-location-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Administrative Assistant Associate", "description": "Administrative Assistant Associate - NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Administrative Assistant Associate - NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Administrative Assistant Associate 503672 NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 30 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Angela Prada, 505-662-2656, angprada@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Position Details Position Title: Administrative Assistant Associate College/Division: Cooperative Extension Service Department: 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Location: NMSU satellite location Offsite Location (if applicable): Los Alamos County Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $16.83 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: Answer phones, emails, and interact with customers who visit the office. Become familiar with the programs and activities offered and disseminate basic information to customers. Provide operational and program support for the Agents. Operate a personal computer to enter data, draft and revise letters and responses to routine inquiries, prepare flyers for events, and reserve meeting spaces for program activities. Assist 4-H Youth Development volunteers and parents with registration, project materials, and policies and procedures. Maintain the county website and social media platforms. Become proficient in the NMSU systems used to perform office procedures. Prepare financial documentation for operational expenses such as utility payments, Agent travel, and program registration. Track monthly office expenditures and maintain procurement card reconciliation. Perform basic administrative duties as needed such as filing, typing, copying, binding, scanning, etc., mail sorting and distribution, and maintain office supplies and equipment. Maintain Civil Rights files and contact reporting. Maintain office hours while Agents are in the field delivering programs. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma + 1 years of relevant experience, or higher degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Dependable, proficient, and team-oriented. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d62f8b11 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Locations NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 9094fc49 Last Name (required) e3a1457b Email (required) f4487883 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Do\u00f1a Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Nursing Clinical Instructor 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940735-DACC NURSING ASSOCIATE DEG PGM DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: College Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) a112912e Last Name (required) aff91ab4 Email (required) e90fbe52 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-artificial-intelligence-education-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education", "description": "Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education 503968 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time Closing at: Oct 22 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Enrico Pontelli, 575-646-2001, epontell@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Position Details Position Title: Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education College/Division: Arts and Sciences College Department: 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualification Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with the National Education Association (NEA). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: Faculty in this position are expected to: \u2022 Conduct innovative, externally funded research on the teaching, learning and application of artificial intelligence, including AI pedagogy, curriculum design, credentialing, and the study of the most effective ways to teach AI to different audiences (students, professionals, educators, and community members). \u2022 Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in artificial intelligence and its applications, contributing to AI curriculum development across disciplines \u2022 Partner with domain specialists across colleges to design and build curricula that embed AI into disciplinary programs of study. \u2022 Lead the development of microcredentials, certificates, and other flexible credentialing pathways in AI. \u2022 Develop and deliver AI training and workforce development programs for diverse audiences within and beyond the university. \u2022 Advise and mentor students at the undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral levels. \u2022 Engage in professional and institutional service, including outreach, committee participation, and strategic initiatives. \u2022 Dedicate a portion of assigned effort to the educational activities of the NMSU Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning, and promote NMSU\u2019s role as a leader in AI education for the state and region. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Education: Earned Ph.D. in a discipline relevant to the position (e.g., artificial intelligence, computing or computational sciences, learning sciences, education, or a relevant AI applied field, e.g., agriculture or manufacturing) by the time of hire. Experience: \u2022 Demonstrated expertise as an AI generalist with a primary focus on teaching, AI curriculum development, credentialing, pedagogy, or educational integration of artificial intelligence. \u2022 Evidence of scholarly productivity or high potential for conducting research in educational frameworks, curriculum design, or pedagogical methods related to AI. \u2022 Experience or strong potential for securing external funding to support computing/AI education and program development. \u2022 Demonstrated commitment to excellence in teaching, curriculum development, and student mentoring. Additional Qualifications: \u2022 Ability to work effectively in a collaborative, multidisciplinary academic environment. \u2022 Preferred experience includes development of microcredentials or professional training programs, integration of AI into non-computing curricula, responsible AI practices, and support of diverse student populations. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Please submit the following documentation with the application: -CV -Statement of Teaching -Statement of Research Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 939e3ba9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 9fcffea8 Last Name (required) 92e05556 Email (required) 655ec867 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Do\u00f1a Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant 