enhance brand awareness and support enrollment objectives. Creative Content Creation and Oversight - Lead the production of engaging and visually compelling campaigns and digital media assets. Ensure all content aligns with NMSU College of Arts & Sciences brand voice, mission, and target audience needs. For example, coordinating the development of promotional videos, student testimonial series, and motion graphics for enrollment campaigns. Digital Media Strategy Development - Develop and execute comprehensive strategies for digital media content aligned with NMSU College of Arts & Sciences overall marketing goals. For example, creating a strategy that integrates video storytelling, photography, and interactive media to elevate brand visibility and foster student engagement. Website Content Management - Maintain and update College of Arts & Sciences web pages and campaign landing pages in accordance with NMSU brand and accessibility standards. Work with departments to publish accurate, timely information about programs, events, and student opportunities; review content and links regularly; and improve page organization, search visibility, and calls to action. Monitor website analytics and recommend updates that strengthen the user experience and support recruitment goals. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 7 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 5 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Experience developing digital marketing content and campaigns for multiple audiences. Strong graphic design, photography, and video production or editing skills, with a portfolio of work. Experience updating web pages through a content management system and writing clear, accessible web content. Strong writing and editing skills for social media, email, web, and print. Ability to manage multiple projects, meet deadlines, and work with departments to gather and verify information. Experience using website and campaign analytics to assess results and recommend improvements. Experience marketing academic programs or recruiting prospective students. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud or comparable design and video tools. Knowledge of search engine optimization, digital accessibility, and brand standards. Knowledge of or experience with Cascade CMS and WordPress, including updating page content, maintaining links, and publishing accessible, brand-consistent web pages. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the peo