ation Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) f456e59a Last Name (required) 54802ae7 Email (required) fa217e3b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/administrative-assistant-associate-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-de89892b-2b07-45aa-8381-ae2c57daf1bc": {"title": "Administrative Assistant Associate", "description": "Administrative Assistant Associate - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Administrative Assistant Associate - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Administrative Assistant Associate 504157 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Alma Meza, 575-646-4022, almeza@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: TPAL seeks an administrative assistant position. This position is a 12-month administrative position that requires on campus in person presence. Position Details Position Title: Administrative Assistant Associate College/Division: College of Hlth, Educ & Soc Trans Department: 350350-SCH OF TCHR PREP, ADMIN & LDSHP Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $16.83 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon external funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: This position supports TPAL leadership and administrative operations across all TPAL programs, with primary responsibility for teacher residency coordination and teacher-pipeline recruitment and outreach. Responsibilities include coordinating and supporting the processing of Teacher Residency stipends; maintaining residency and grant-related records; assisting with data collection, reporting, and survey administration; and supporting residency meetings, professional learning, and Communities of Practice. The position also plans, coordinates, and attends recruitment and community outreach events; supports recruitment efforts across TPAL programs; and communicates with prospective and current students, faculty, school personnel, and community partners. Additional responsibilities include providing school-wide administrative support to TPAL leadership, faculty, staff, and students and developing proficiency in NMSU systems used to perform office procedures. The position requires strong organizational, communication, customer-service, and technology skills; exceptional attention to detail; and the ability to manage multiple events, deadlines, grant activities, and administrative responsibilities simultaneously. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma + 1 years of relevant experience, or higher degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Experience providing administrative support in a university, school district, or other educational setting. \u2022 Experience providing program coordination support in a university, school district, or other educational setting. \u2022 Experience supporting educator preparation, student recruitment and retention activities, and other outreach initiatives. \u2022 Experience working collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and community partners. \u2022 Experience coordinating events, meetings, workshops, including scheduling, communications, registration, purchasing, and on-site logistics. \u2022 Experience collecting, maintaining, and reporting program or grant-related data. \u2022 Proficiency with university information systems and Microsoft 365 applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, Teams, SharePoint, and OneDrive. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and professionally with diverse constituencies. \u2022 Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. \u2022 Ability and willingness to travel periodically for recruitment, outreach, and community-engagement activities, including occasional evening or weekend events. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c3fbc6f5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 350350-SCH OF TCHR PREP, ADMIN & LDSHP 350350-SCH OF TCHR PREP, ADMIN & LDSHP Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) a4f04878 Last Name (required) efbc150c Email (required) df15c66c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Do\u00f1a Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Nursing Clinical Instructor 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940735-DACC NURSING ASSOCIATE DEG PGM DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: College Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) ec4c5c6a Last Name (required) 62c250d2 Email (required) b18f71fc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/program-specialist-senior-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-1d88a29a-ec8c-478f-984e-f6ed46be2b3e": {"title": "Program Specialist Senior", "description": "Program Specialist Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Program Specialist Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Program Specialist Senior 504153 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Samantha Lish, 575-646-1726, slish@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: **THIS IS A ONE YEAR APPOINTMENT. MAY BE EXTENDED CONTINGENT UPON FUNDING.** The Jornada Basin Long-Term Ecological Research (LTER) Program requires a Program Specialist, Sr to help continue the productivity of its research projects. Working under the direction of the Lead Technician and the Site Manager, the successful candidate carries out the program's long-term measurements and the associated field and laboratory work, enters and checks the resulting data, coordinates field schedules and equipment, and helps keep the program's field instrumentation and wireless data network in service. Position Details Position Title: Program Specialist Senior College/Division: Agricultural Experiment Station Department: 317250-JORNADA EXPER RANGE HEADQUARTERS Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon external funding Standard Work Schedule: Shift: Other Shift If Not a Standard Work Schedule: May work early mornings, evenings, and weekends. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Field and Laboratory \u2022 Collects data related to plant ecology, aeolian studies, hydrology, animal ecology, soils, UAV operations, and wireless data acquisition/climatology. \u2022 Supports the Lead Technician and Site Manager in carrying out LTER long-term studies associated with vegetation measurements. Plans and implements associated projects in collaboration with researchers. \u2022 Sample processing, cleaning equipment, checking/entering data and maintaining appropriate documentation. \u2022 Trains staff on plant identification. Maintains herbarium voucher collection. Data Entry, Management, and Documentation \u2022 Enters, checks, and corrects field and sensor data; maintains the documentation and metadata that keep long-term datasets complete and traceable. \u2022 Compiles and summarizes program activity data in support of reports to researchers and funding sources. Scheduling, Organization, and Coordination \u2022 Coordinates field schedules, vehicles, supplies, and equipment for seasonal measurement campaigns. \u2022 Assists in allocating, training, and directing the work of assigned staff and students, including promotion and enforcement of internal procedures, safe work practices, and data-collection protocols. \u2022 Coordinates program needs with other agencies and groups working at the site and serves as a day-to-day point of contact on field operations. Equipment, Vehicles, and Wireless Network \u2022 Maintains the program's wireless data network and associated field data-acquisition equipment; troubleshoots connectivity, sensor, and datalogger problems at remote field sites and arranges repairs. \u2022 Performs routine maintenance, repair, and inventory of field equipment, sampling gear, and program vehicles; keeps vehicles serviced and field-ready and reports mechanical problems for repair. \u2022 Supports UAV operations and other instrumented data collection as assigned. \u2022 Performs miscellaneous job-related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 4 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 2 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: \u2022 Significant field experience in plant identification, measurement methodologies, and use of dichotomous keys. \u2022 Knowledge of Chihuahuan Desert flora and fauna. \u2022 Experience working in a lab environment, and field experience related to this LTER program or a comparable long-term ecological research program. \u2022 Demonstrated skills in training and directing the work of assigned staff. \u2022 Experience entering, checking, and documenting ecological datasets. \u2022 Proficiency with Microsoft Office, and experience with ArcGIS and R for data management, mapping, and analysis. \u2022 Working familiarity with field data-acquisition systems \u2014 dataloggers, sensors, telemetry, and wireless networking \u2014 sufficient to keep remote stations reporting. \u2022 Current FAA Part 107 Remote Pilot Certificate, or the ability to obtain one, in support of the program's UAV operations. \u2022 Experience operating 4x4 vehicles on unimproved roads and off-road desert terrain. \u2022 Self-motivated, flexible, possess strong supervisory and organizational abilities. \u2022 Enjoy working under desert field conditions with high heat and sun exposure. \u2022 Work reliably both independently and as part of a team. \u2022 Establish and maintain effective working relationships with associates and principal investigators. \u2022 Be comfortable working safely with moderately hazardous materials. \u2022 Communicate well both verbally and in writing. \u2022 Be able to coordinate needs with other agencies/groups Special Certification/Licensure: \u2022 This is a field position and the work can be physically strenuous. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds of equipment and supplies over uneven desert terrain. \u2022 Ability to work outdoors during hot or cold, windy weather. \u2022 Valid Driver's License (needed to obtain NMSU Driver's Permit). Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work involves moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises. Physical Effort: Moderate physical activity. Lifting Requirements: Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing, or pulling required of objects up to 50 pounds. Risk: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1ff956e9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 317250-JORNADA EXPER RANGE HEADQUARTERS 317250-JORNADA EXPER RANGE HEADQUARTERS Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) b4a499c8 Last Name (required) 0f23c608 Email