 of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Nursing Clinical Instructor 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940735-DACC NURSING ASSOCIATE DEG PGM DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: College Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) ef263e3d Last Name (required) 390d1078 Email (required) 712079c5 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/lab-coordinator-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-d2e5214f-4630-4d47-8281-c5d5cef8edf2": {"title": "Lab Coordinator", "description": "Lab Coordinator - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Lab Coordinator - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Lab Coordinator 504138 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Luis Sabillon Galeas, 575-646-3936, lsabillo@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The NMSU Food Safety Laboratory is seeking a Laboratory Coordinator to support the operation, quality management, and continued growth of an ISO/IEC 17025-accredited food safety testing laboratory. The position will coordinate laboratory activities and provide technical and quality assurance support for food microbiology testing, laboratory documentation, quality control, internal audits, corrective actions, and accreditation requirements. The successful candidate will play a key role in maintaining and continually improving the laboratory\u2019s ISO/IEC 17025 quality management system while supporting day-to-day laboratory operations, testing activities, personnel coordination, and client service. This position offers an opportunity to work in a dynamic, student-supported laboratory environment focused on food safety testing, research, and applied services for industry, government, and other stakeholders. Position Details Position Title: Lab Coordinator College/Division: Agricultural Experiment Station Department: 317775-BIO SECURITYAND FOOD SAFETY CENTER Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: \u2022 Coordinate daily operations of the NMSU Food Safety Laboratory, including sample processing, testing activities, workflow, and laboratory resources. \u2022 Maintain and continually improve the laboratory\u2019s ISO/IEC 17025 quality management system and ensure compliance with accreditation requirements. \u2022 Coordinate quality assurance and quality control activities, including document control, recordkeeping, quality monitoring, corrective actions, and continual improvement. \u2022 Support internal audits, external assessments, surveillance visits, proficiency testing, and other laboratory accreditation activities. \u2022 Review laboratory documentation and testing records to ensure accuracy, completeness, traceability, and compliance with established procedures. \u2022 Support development, revision, verification, validation, and implementation of laboratory methods, SOPs, and quality procedures. \u2022 Perform and/or oversee food microbiology testing and related laboratory activities within the laboratory\u2019s scope of services. \u2022 Coordinate training and provide technical guidance to laboratory personnel, students, and other staff on testing methods, quality requirements, and laboratory procedures. \u2022 Support equipment calibration, maintenance, verification, inventory, and associated documentation. \u2022 Assist with sample receiving, accessioning, tracking, testing, reporting, and records management. \u2022 Support laboratory safety, biosafety, and contamination-control practices. \u2022 Assist with client services, laboratory projects, research activities, and other operational needs of the Food Safety Laboratory. \u2022 Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 2 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in food science, microbiology, biology, or a closely related field; professional experience in a food, environmental, clinical, or other analytical laboratory; demonstrated experience with laboratory quality assurance and quality control programs; experience developing, implementing, maintaining, or continually improving an ISO/IEC 17025 quality management system; experience supporting laboratory accreditation, internal audits, external assessments, corrective actions, and proficiency testing; knowledge of food microbiology, microbiological testing methods, molecular methods, and laboratory quality control practices; experience with laboratory information management systems, technical documentation, equipment calibration, method verification/validation, and data review; experience training and supervising laboratory personnel, students, or technicians; and strong organizational, analytical, communication, and problem-solving skills. Special Certification/Licensure: Certification as a laboratory quality professional, such as ASQ Certified Quality Auditor (CQA), Certified Quality Improvement Associate (CQIA), or related credential, is preferred but not required. Formal training or certification in ISO/IEC 17025, laboratory auditing, quality management systems, food microbiology, biosafety, or related areas is also preferred. No specific professional license is required. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed indoors. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 0d8be2ef Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 317775-BIO SECURITYAND FOOD SAFETY CENTER 317775-BIO SECURITYAND FOOD SAFETY CENTER Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 35fd7fa7 Last Name (required) fa599462 Email (required) 854e39f1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Do\u00f1a Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant Professor \u2013 Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Nursing Clinical Instructor 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940735-DACC NURSING ASSOCIATE DEG PGM DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: College Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) d98de4b1 Last Name (required) 4a25a380 Email (required) e3636d39 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/alcc-director-library-services-alamogordo-community-college-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "ALCC Director Library Services", "description": "ALCC Director Library Services - Alamogordo Community College, New Mexico, United States ALCC Director Library Services - Alamogordo Community College, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode ALCC Director Library Services 503946 Alamogordo Community College, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Dr. Mark P. Cal, Chief Executive and Academic Officer, mcal@nmsu.edu, 575.439.3621 Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: New Mexico State University\u2013Alamogordo is seeking an experienced and service-focused Manager, Library Services to lead the day-to-day operations and continued development of library services supporting students, faculty, staff, and the broader campus community. This position provides leadership across collection development, acquisitions, cataloging, circulation, reference services, and library programming. The Manager will develop and implement effective policies and procedures, supervise and support library staff, provide training, and foster a welcoming and responsive library environment. The ideal candidate will be a collaborative leader who can assess community information needs, build strong relationships with faculty and students, and identify opportunities to enhance library resources and services. The Manager will also stay current with emerging trends, technologies, and best practices in library science to ensure the library continues to evolve with the needs of its users. Join NMSU\u2013Alamogordo and help shape a library that serves as a vital center for learning, discovery, and community engagement. Position Details Position Title: ALCC Director Library Services College/Division: ALCC Alamogordo CC Department: 920760-ALCC LIBRARY Location: Alamogordo Community College Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate With Experience Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Shift: Other Shift If Not a Standard Work Schedule: May require occasional work in the evenings or weekends, as determined by department need. Job Duties and Responsibilities: Manages and oversees library services, including collection development, acquisitions, cataloging, circulation, reference services, and library programming. Develops and implements policies and procedures to ensure efficient operation of the library. Supervises library staff, provides training and support, and evaluates performance. Collaborates with faculty, students, and other stakeholders to assess and meet the information needs of the community. Stays current on trends and best practices in library science and technology to enhance services and resources. Attend statewide meetings. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Bachelor\u2019s degree in any field and four (4) years of progressively responsible experience in library services, information services, or a related area, including at least one (1) year of supervisory or lead experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in a related field and Five (5) years of professional experience related to the job duties and responsibilities as outlined. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d8a5808c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 920760-ALCC LIBRARY 920760-ALCC LIBRARY Locations Alamogordo Community College, New Mexico, United States Alamogordo Community College, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 6f224e8a Last Name (required) 75b86110 Email (required) 5125406f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Do\u00f1a Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply