s for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 5e8e5ed1 Last Name (required) f7a520a3 Email (required) 7d865975 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/lead-cashier-dona-ana-community-college-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Lead Cashier", "description": "Lead Cashier - Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Lead Cashier - Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Lead Cashier 504210 Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: McKenna Garcia, 575-527-7550, mkgarci@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Position Details Position Title: Lead Cashier College/Division: DACC Dona Ana CC Department: 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS Location: Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Offsite Location (if applicable): DACC East Mesa Campus Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $17.85 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: DACC East Mesa Campus Job Duties and Responsibilities: This is a customer service driven position in that the cashier area provides support to students, faculty, and staff. This position must adhere to cash handling guidelines as well as financial system guidelines. Cashiers are responsible for receiving and providing documentation for a variety of payment methods and related transactions, to include, but not limited to: Student tuition payments, student club payments, third-party payments, etc. Daily transaction reconciliations are required for cash reports, balancing of cash drawers, to include cash, credit cards, checks, etc. Making deposits and reordering of currency and coin is included in daily reconciliations. The ability to investigate and correct reconciliations which do not balance is paramount. System and financial knowledge is required for posting daily transactions, posting to student accounts, preparing journal entries, preparing reconciliations, creating receipts, making deposits, routine billing, balancing accounts, etc. Providing information and training to other DACC campus cashiers and the ability to answer inquiries regarding tuition and fees, providing resources to assist students, and deposit and withdrawal guidance is necessary as customer support. Interactions with third-party sponsors and calculations are required for student financial support reporting. The ability to create financial reports, troubleshoot and analyze data is required. Provides data and information regarding customer satisfaction and college services review. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma + 3 years of relevant experience or an Associate\u2019s Degree + 1 year of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of cash handling protocols and financial/accounting procedures. Ability to analyze, solve problems and make correction using computerized information systems is required. Knowledge Excel, Word, Teams, and Zoom is required. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 97573ec1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS Locations Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 1964556e Last Name (required) c21f31f8 Email (required) 111d9576 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 81848766 Last Name (required) 39f2e022 Email (required) 55470654 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/associate-dean-of-students-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Associate Dean of Students", "description": "Associate Dean of Students - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Associate Dean of Students - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Associate Dean of Students 504199 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Nicki Halopka, 575-646-1722, nhalopka@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Position Details Position Title: Associate Dean of Students College/Division: Provost Office Department: 520830-STUDENT LIFE Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $53,165 - $67,786.96 commensurate with experience Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: Under the direction of the Senior Associate Dean of Students, the Associate Dean of Students provides leadership and oversight for the university\u2019s academic and non-academic student conduct processes, including serving as a Title IX sanctioning officer and alternate hearing officer for serious violations involving harassment, substance use, and interpersonal violence. The Associate Dean coordinates the university\u2019s Academic Integrity and Student Organization Conduct programs, oversees use of the Maxient conduct management system, and ensures training and support for faculty, staff, and student conduct partners. The Associate Dean plays a critical role in promoting ethical decision-making, harm reduction, and behavioral accountability while supporting student rights and due process in a developmentally focused framework. This position collaborates closely with academic departments, housing, student involvement, campus safety offices, and institutional compliance partners, and contributes to student well-being through participation in the CARE and Behavioral Intervention Teams. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 6 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 4 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Education: Master\u2019s degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, Counseling, Educational Leadership, Law, or a related field. Experience: At least three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in student conduct, student affairs, case management, or a related area within a higher education setting. Demonstrated experience adjudicating student conduct or Title IX cases and working with behavioral intervention or CARE teams. Knowledge and Skills Comprehensive understanding of FERPA, Title IX, Clery Act, and student conduct legal frameworks. Experience using and managing conduct database systems (e.g., Maxient). Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, including ability to effectively manage sensitive conversations and serve diverse populations. Strong administrative, organizational, and case management skills Ability to collaborate with cross-functional teams and campus stakeholders. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 7ffcdd0a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 520830-STUDENT LIFE 520830-STUDENT LIFE Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) fed2d575 Last Name (required) 53d143f1 Email (required) ed490bcc Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 627fef6c Last Name (required) 4f4f7cb4 Email (required) 8e27a948 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/program-coordinator-senior-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Program Coordinator Senior", "description": "Program Coordinator Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Program Coordinator Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Program Coordinator Senior 504207 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Mari Langford, mlangfor@nmsu.edu, 575-646-1906 Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Position Details Position Title: Program Coordinator Senior College/Division: Arts and Sciences College Department: 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon external funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Occasional evening and weekends may be required. Job Duties and Responsibilities: The coordinator will develop and deliver educational programs, support teacher professional learning, and build partnerships connecting IAAM\u2019s expertise with K\u201312 school needs. This role translates AI and machine learning concepts into accessible, age-appropriate learning experiences that strengthen AI literacy, critical thinking, creativity, and problem-solving. A central focus of this position is promoting the responsible and ethical use of AI in K\u201312 education. The coordinator will help educators and students make informed decisions about when and how to use AI, protect student privacy, recognize bias and misinformation, acknowledge AI assistance, and preserve human judgment. Programming will emphasize equitable access, age-appropriate practices, and the use of AI to support learning, creativity, and independent thinking. \u2022 Plan, coordinate, and evaluate AI education initiatives for K\u201312 schools, including classroom activities, after-school programs, workshops, and summer learning opportunities. \u2022 Facilitate professional learning that helps educators understand AI, assess its usefulness, and integrate appropriate tools into instruction. \u2022 Support teachers and IAAM faculty and specialists to develop and deploy curriculum resources covering AI literacy, foundational machine learning concepts, and practical applications across subject areas. \u2022 Create hands-on learning experiences that help students explore how AI systems work, examine their limitations, and critically evaluate AI-generated content. \u2022 Build and maintain partnerships with schools, districts, community organizations, and other stakeholders to identify needs and expand participation. \u2022 Organize family and community outreach events that make AI concepts accessible and connect learning with educational and career opportunities. \u2022 Coordinate program schedules, materials, communications, and logistics, including support for participating faculty, student mentors, and volunteers. \u2022 Collect educator feedback and program data to assess learning outcomes, document impact, and improve programming. \u2022 Contribute to grant proposals, reports, and outreach materials supporting IAAM\u2019s K\u201312 education initiatives. \u2022 Stay informed about developments in AI education and update resources to reflect changing tools. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's degree + 4 years of relevant experience or a bachelor\u2019s degree + 2 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Skill in organizing resources and establishing priorities. Ability to develop and maintain record-keeping systems and procedures. Ability to provide coordination and implementation projects. Knowledge of fiscal processes internal to NMSU. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert dad4fd55 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 0122ba5b Last Name (required) 11deb438 Email (required) 14762ce6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 613d17f1 Last Name (required) c26b6f0d Email (required) e67351d1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/administrative-assistant-intermediate-dona-ana-community-college-new-mexico-united-states-64c16cee-758d-4f64-8c95-00e51ddcfad8": {"title": "Administrative Assistant Intermediate", "description": "Administrative Assistant Intermediate - Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Administrative Assistant Intermediate - Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Administrative Assistant Intermediate 504201 Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Kathy Shreffler; 575-527-7700; kshreffl@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Administrative Assistant III Position Details Position Title: Administrative Assistant Intermediate College/Division: DACC Dona Ana CC Department: 941230-DACC FACILITIES SUPP Location: Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $17.85 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: This Position not only provides Administrative Support for the Facilities Manager but is also the Main Administrative support for four Facilities Supervisors, Security supervisor with 11 direct reports, Assistant Manager and maintenance supervisor with 11 direct reports, Custodial Supervisor A, with 11 Direct reports and Custodial Supervisor B with 13 Direct reports. Facilities has a total of 49 Employees Standard Duties include; - Manages the Facilities Information, Services and Work order Desk, we are open Monday- Friday 8am to 5pm - Customer Service; Answers phone calls, assists with helping customers submit work orders, advises customers on proper procedures with procurement issues, and deals with a wide variety of Customer Concerns. Provides assistance to contractors and vendors providing services to DACC. Manages our Computerized work order system (School Dude) and assigns work orders to appropriate staff. - Receives keys and cards from employees leaving and distributes keys and cards to new employees. Assists customers with any issues they are having with Keys or electronic key cards. - Responsible for ordering and receiving in Aggie Mart, receiving for PO\u2019s and open Po\u2019s, as well as reconciliation of P-Cards for Five Employees. Due to the nature of Facilities repairs, renovations, and cleaning services, ordering and receiving are done on an almost daily basis. - Responsible for management and updates for the yearly NMSU Space survey. This survey identifies every space in every building at all DACC Campuses and is reviewed and updated Yearly for the NMSU Space management Department. - Responsible for Yearly inventory for all Facilities Equipment. Has assisted other departments and divisions with their inventory as well. - Manages Hiring and supervision of work study students. - Provides Assistance to customer requests for small furniture needs, Desks, chairs, File cabinets and bookshelves makes arrangements for ordering and delivery and set up. Assists Facilities Manager with Large Furniture Projects and Renovations. - Manages logistics for Special event set up, works with customers to make sure their needs are met. Provides information and support for Custodial and Maintenance Staff for special event\u2019s needs. - Manages Deliveries to the Facilities Loading dock and receiving area. Informs Customers and makes arrangements for local delivery to the appropriate space. - Serves on search committees on a regular basis and other Campus Committees by invitation and need. - Processes all Travel and Training requests for the department. Makes sure all proper procedures are followed. - Assists all Departmental employees with computer access issues, on-boarding trainings, compliance training, banner, time keeping, e-mail issues, and work order system access. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma + 3 years of relevant experience or an Associate's Degree + 1 year of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Bi-Lingual English/Spanish preferred. Proficient in Microsoft programs, Word, Excel, ability to set up meetings in Teams or Zoom. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 8dbe5de2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 941230-DACC FACILITIES SUPP 941230-DACC FACILITIES SUPP Locations Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) a7425d5e Last Name (required) 50940b2a Email (required) e80f3ef1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 5563c191 Last Name (required) 53fca9d1 Email (required) e4321aba Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/production-manager-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Production Manager", "description": "Production Manager - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Production Manager - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Production Manager 504205 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Nancy Holguin Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: Production Manager \u2013 KRWG Public Media at New Mexico State University in beautiful Las Cruces is looking for a Production Manager to lead our dynamic multimedia production team across all platforms. We\u2019re looking for a skilled communicator, director, team builder, creative thinker, an Adobe Creative Suite expert, and someone that is as comfortable in the studio as they are in the field. In addition, top-notch studio & EFP lighting skills and the ability to train and oversee student employees are required. This full-time position will also oversee and manage our television production facilities, technology, equipment, and will work alongside the content team to produce original, compelling content. Position Details Position Title: Production Manager College/Division: President's Office Department: 331120-KRWG TELEVISION Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $53,165.80 target entry to commensurate with qualifications Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Production Manager leads a dynamic multimedia production team across traditional broadcast and emerging digital platforms. This position requires strong, hands-on expertise in television and multimedia production, along with the ability to mentor and develop professional staff and students in a collaborative learning environment. The Production Manager will oversee all aspects of television and multimedia production, including production facilities, technology, equipment, and workflows, while maintaining high standards for technical excellence and production quality. Working closely with the content team, the Production Manager will help create original, compelling content for broadcast and digital audiences. A key focus of this position is expanding and strengthening the organization\u2019s digital presence. The successful candidate will understand how to adapt and develop content specifically for online audiences, with an emphasis on increasing engagement across digital and social media platforms while preserving the high production values associated with traditional television. Plans, directs, and supervises television and multimedia production activities, project development, personnel, facilities, and equipment. Provides leadership in both traditional broadcast production and the development of digital content strategies designed to grow online audience engagement. \u2022 Supervises, mentors, and develops departmental employees and student staff, fostering a collaborative environment that supports professional growth and hands-on learning. \u2022 Manages all production activities and operations, including studio, remote, broadcast, and digital productions. \u2022 Oversees the scheduling and effective use of personnel, facilities, technology, and production equipment. \u2022 Ensures the proper setup and teardown of staging, lighting, audio, cameras, and other technical elements required for high-quality multimedia productions. \u2022 Directs technical production staff and participates in studio and remote production activities as needed. \u2022 Maintains high production standards, technical quality, and consistency across traditional broadcast and digital content. \u2022 Works collaboratively with content and editorial teams to develop and produce original, compelling programming for television, web, social media, and other digital platforms. \u2022 Identifies opportunities to enhance digital storytelling and develop content specifically designed to engage online audiences. \u2022 Helps grow the organization\u2019s digital presence by incorporating innovative production techniques and strategies that increase audience engagement and reach. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 4 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 2 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Any equivalent combination of education, training and/or experience as approved by Human Resource Services. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a related field and Two (2) years of professional experience related to the job duties duties and responsibilities as outlined. Special Certification/Licensure: Applicants are required to submit a link to an online portfolio or work samples showcasing their recent work. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 656a7f5f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 331120-KRWG TELEVISION 331120-KRWG TELEVISION Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 32fd049d Last Name (required) 3fafe38b Email (required) 1710b847 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) cd9d1243 Last Name (required) a1f9e417 Email (required) 20828ccb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you 