Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Assistant Dean of Students (Student Conduct Officer) is responsible for administering the student conduct and academic integrity processes at New Mexico State University in accordance with institutional policies and procedures. This role promotes a safe, respectful, and inclusive learning environment by fostering student accountability and supporting holistic development through education, restorative practices, and conflict resolution. The Assistant Dean collaborates with students, faculty, staff, and campus partners to provide training, guidance, and leadership on conduct-related matters and serves as a primary institutional resource for addressing behavioral concerns. The position also serves as a liaison to faculty and the Faculty Senate to address academic integrity concerns and contribute to the development and revision of related university policies. This position supports the broader mission of student success through strategic initiatives, policy development, and data-informed assessment. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 2 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, Counseling, Educational Leadership, Law, or a closely related field. Two (2) years of progressively responsible experience in student conduct, residence life, student affairs, or a related area within a higher education setting. Demonstrated knowledge of student development theory, student conduct processes, and federal and state compliance laws (e.g., FERPA, Title IX, Clery Act). Experience interpreting and applying complex university policies, facilitating investigations or hearings, and working with diverse student populations. Five (5) years of progressively responsible experience. Experience serving as a conduct officer at a college or university. Familiarity with and administrative experience using conduct databases such as Maxient (including report generation and data analytics). Demonstrated success collaborating with faculty governance bodies such as Faculty Senate on academic integrity or conduct-related policy matters. Experience with restorative justice, conflict resolution, or alternative dispute resolution in a student conduct setting. Supervisory experience of professional or student staff. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 4c00c924 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 520830-STUDENT LIFE 520830-STUDENT LIFE Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 2be4a6e4 Last Name (required) fdba37fd Email (required) 60577ec9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 0b6a3ad9 Last Name (required) fe952fc8 Email (required) c6cd3f61 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/nmda-public-affairs-specialist-intermediate-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "NMDA Public Affairs Specialist Intermediate", "description": "NMDA Public Affairs Specialist Intermediate - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States NMDA Public Affairs Specialist Intermediate - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode NMDA Public Affairs Specialist Intermediate 504190 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Cheryl Mason-Herrera, 575-646-7523, cmason@nmda.nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The New Mexico Department of Agriculture (NMDA) works for the benefit of the state\u2019s citizens and supports the viability of agriculture and affiliated industries. NMDA promotes food protection, a uniform and fair marketplace, and global marketing and economic development; supports the beneficial use of natural resources; and works cooperatively with public and private sector entities. Opportunities for excellence abound, and NMDA staff dedicate themselves to proactive service in fulfilling the department\u2019s mission. Each division plays an important role in carrying out the goals and objectives. Our rich agricultural history, culture, and traditions are addressed through new and innovative approaches using the latest in science, technology, and economic strategies. In New Mexico, we contribute to the safest, most affordable, and nutritious food supply on the globe. NMDA is a constitutional agency organized under the Board of Regents of New Mexico State University (NMSU). This unique relationship creates efficiencies and opportunities for New Mexico\u2019s food and agriculture sector as well as service and outreach opportunities for NMSU, making NMDA an integral part of the university. NMDA/NMSU is an equal opportunity employer. Position Details Position Title: NMDA Public Affairs Specialist Intermediate College/Division: New Mexico Dept of Agriculture Department: 180001-NEW MEXICO DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTUR Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Entry $ 59,965.78 - Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: Under the direction of the NMDA Division Director and general supervision of the NMDA Public Affairs Asst, Sr., key tasks include writing and editing a variety of materials, such as press releases and media content. Plans and creates social media content for all of the department's platforms; provides analytics reports for social media; writes and edits social media posts; and edits news releases and other materials. The position also entails translating news releases and other documents to Spanish; handling video production; assisting with photography; and supporting the coordination of event planning, implementation, and evaluation. Establishing and nurturing relationships with media representatives, the public, and key stakeholders is crucial, as is assisting with media relations. The role involves resolving equipment problems and failures as they arise. Additionally, this position handles internal communications to keep staff informed and ensures adherence to relevant laws and regulations. Engaging with advertising clients and supporting public relations initiatives are integral aspects of the job. May represent the organization at community and business meetings, as well as participate in committees and task forces. Assisting in the creation and execution of communication strategies and processes that align with the organization's obligations-including those that encompass legislative and rulemaking obligations and processes-its objectives, and brand identity is essential. Support for the organization's social media platforms is necessary to enhance engagement. This role also involves maintaining mailing lists, contributing to crisis communication efforts, and providing guidance on public relations matters. May perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 7 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 5 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Any equivalent combination of education, training and/or experience as approved by Human Resource Services. Preferred Qualifications: Spanish language translation Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 863af3c9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 180001-NEW MEXICO DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTUR 180001-NEW MEXICO DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTUR Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 462e7bb0 Last Name (required) a336766a Email (required) 38ff50d7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) d92f63bc Last Name (required) 3cb1b4f6 Email (required) 7ff4790f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/director-museum-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Director Museum", "description": "Director Museum - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Director Museum - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Director Museum 504189 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Enrico Pontelli, epontell@nmsu.edu, (575) 646-6239 Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The University Art Museum at New Mexico State University is seeking a Director. Position Details Position Title: Director Museum College/Division: Arts and Sciences College Department: 330110-UNIVERSITY ART MUSEUM Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: New Mexico State University (NMSU) seeks an engaging, dynamic, and qualified individual for the position of Director of the University Art Museum (UAM) to coordinate and realize exhibitions and programming that advance the mission of the UAM and the university, while heightening the UAM\u2019s visibility in the region and nationally. The Director plans and manages the UAM\u2019s rotating exhibitions (9 to 12 per year) with the support of the Art Museum Manager; raises, manages, and optimizes funding from diverse sources while building lasting donor relationships and ensuring responsible, sustainable stewardship of the organization\u2019s resources; oversees financial, facility, technology, marketing, communications, and human resource functions within the UAM; and streamlines operations to best meet organizational needs. The Director also oversees the NMSU Permanent Art Collection, budgeting, and acquisitions with the support of the Collections Curator; trains undergraduate and graduate student employees; researches and prepares grant proposals; and serves as a liaison and resource for the NMSU campus and broader community. NMSU is the state\u2019s land-grant university, serving the educational needs of New Mexico\u2019s diverse population through programs of education, research, extension education, and public service. The NMSU University Art Museum is housed on the main campus of NMSU in Las Cruces, NM in the El Paso del Norte Region which includes El Paso, Texas and Ciudad Juarez, Mexico. The director reports to the Dean of the College of Arts and Sciences and maintains a close working relationship with various NMSU executive positions and the NMSU Foundation, and implements policies and procedures established in accordance with the provisions in the by-laws and in accordance with American Alliance of Museums (AAM) National Standards and Best Practices. The UAM is the premier contemporary visual arts facility in Southern New Mexico and holds the world\u2019s largest collection of 19th century Mexican retablos as well as modern & contemporary collections which include photographs, paintings, prints and graphics, book art, metals/jewelry, sculpture and ceramics. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 10 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 8 years of relevant experience. Master's degree or higher preferred. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Resonance and or connection with the unique southwest and borderland region; identification with the mission and values of the UAM, including a deep appreciation for the full scope and breadth of its collections and assets; capacity to define, communicate, and execute clear priorities while operating within the framework of a public, state-funded institution; demonstrated administrative competency; experience in supervising staff; leadership within a collaborative environment; experience and success in grant writing; demonstrated ability to develop and implement strategic initiatives, manage multiple priorities, and collaborate effectively across departments and areas of expertise; experience overseeing, training and teaching students in a wide range of museum areas and skills. Knowledge of museum and curatorial practices, including exhibit preparation required. Teaching experience is a plus. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 3648f40b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 330110-UNIVERSITY ART MUSEUM 330110-UNIVERSITY ART MUSEUM Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 84af7582 Last Name (required) 048da9da Email (required) ebfefb8a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD 