Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) ff67cb51 Last Name (required) b694475f Email (required) 1933dced Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/electronics-technician-associate-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-a2b56037-e331-47e9-82e3-14fd5bee1cbb": {"title": "Electronics Technician Associate", "description": "Electronics Technician Associate - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Electronics Technician Associate - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Electronics Technician Associate 504195 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Brooke Yaksich, psl_hrs@psl.nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: Join the team as an Electronics Technician Associate! Position Details Position Title: Electronics Technician Associate College/Division: Physical Science Laboratory Department: 470551-PSL ISC PRODUCTION Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $19.28 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.00 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon external funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: Assemble printed wiring boards, cable connectors and harnesses for installation onto the telemetry systems. Perform Electrical and RF testing of telemetry systems as per established testing procedures. Package and ship telemetry hardware and/or systems with associated documentation. Perform general mechanical/electrical assembly techniques and other related duties as required. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma + 1 years of relevant experience, or higher degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Special Certification/Licensure: Ability to obtain a DoD clearance and maintain clearance throughout employment. This position is subject to random drug testing in compliance with its drug-free workforce requirements. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work involves moderate exposure to unusual elements, such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises. Physical Effort: Moderate physical activity. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds or standing and/or walking for more than four (4) hours per day. Risk: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 0dbddcc9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 470551-PSL ISC PRODUCTION 470551-PSL ISC PRODUCTION Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 4342be14 Last Name (required) 9c928eb1 Email (required) f459c33d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 71765038 Last Name (required) f8a16138 Email (required) de3c689b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/program-manager-senior-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-88f161bc-7c3a-4aaf-9e7f-2ef2fadce18d": {"title": "Program Manager Senior", "description": "Program Manager Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Program Manager Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Program Manager Senior 504176 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Wanda Tamez, (575) 646-2755, wtamez@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The NMSU STEM Outreach Center is seeking a Program Manager Senior for OST Programs to advance STEM+ education across southern New Mexico by providing high-quality professional learning for PreK\u201312 educators, developing engaging inquiry-based curriculum, and supporting schools and communities in creating impactful STEM+ out-of-school time programs. Position Details Position Title: Program Manager Senior College/Division: College of Hlth, Educ & Soc Trans Department: 350410-INST FOR EXCEL IN MATH & SCIENCE ED Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $59,965.78; Commensurate with Experience. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon external funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Program Manager Senior position serves as assistant director for the STEM Outreach Center at New Mexico State University (NMSU) to plan, coordinate, implement, and evaluate out-of-school-time (OST) STEM initiatives, including after-school programs, summer camps, and family engagement events. The position works closely with the Executive Director to manage day-to-day operations of assigned grant-funded programs, ensuring high-quality delivery and alignment with approved program goals, University policies, and grant requirements. The manager develops operational plans, implements approved procedures, and recommends program improvements. The manager coordinates with principals, community partners, and University personnel; supports and supervises assigned Center program staff; monitors budgets and expenditures in collaboration with the fiscal manager; and coordinates timely completion of grant deliverables. Responsibilities include preparing and coordinating Memoranda of Understanding (MOUs) for appropriate review and approval, initiating and supporting grant proposal and funding development, and monitoring program outcomes. The manager track participation, implementation, outcomes, and required deliverables in collaboration with the STEM Outreach Center\u2019s Data team; provides regular reports to the Executive Director; and recommend improvements based on findings and partner feedback. The Program Manager provides regular updates and recommendations to the Executive Director and refers decisions requiring executive or institutional approval through established channels. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 9 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 7 years of relevant experience. Master's degree or higher preferred. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in STEM Education, School Administration, or related field; 5+ years experience in developing district and school partnerships for out-of-school time programs; experience in developing STEM-based K-12 OST curriculum. School of education grant administration experience preferred. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds or standing and/or walking for more than four (4) hours per day. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert f28a621e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 350410-INST FOR EXCEL IN MATH & SCIENCE ED 350410-INST FOR EXCEL IN MATH & SCIENCE ED Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) d9b364e3 Last Name (required) 50f79ff9 Email (required) 1f4e7423 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Commu