n Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Position Details Position Title: Admissions Advisor College/Division: GRCC Grants CC Department: 950850-GRCC STUDENT SERVICES CTR Location: Grants Community College Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: 43,908.80-49,397.27 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Shift: Other Shift If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Normal 8-5 M-F 40 hours per week. Work schedules will be adjusted as needed to accommodate recruitment events occurring outside of regular business hours (8:00 a.m.\u20135:00 p.m.). Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Admissions Advisor at NMSU Grants supports recruitment, outreach, and enrollment through regular high school visits, community engagement, and admissions advising. This position assists prospective students and families with admissions, academic programs, financial aid, and enrollment while supporting dual credit and campus recruitment initiatives. Outreach & Recruitment \u2022 Visit high schools across the greater Cibola County area to promote the NMSU Grants academic program and to support recruitment initiatives. \u2022 Conduct campus tours, formal and informal presentations, and other recruitment activities. Student, Family & Engagement \u2022 Advises prospective students and families regarding educational opportunities and options, admissions, new student orientation, registration, and related university requirements, policies, and procedures. \u2022 Responds to inquiries from prospective students regarding admissions, academic programs, financial aid, and other enrollment-related topics. \u2022 Guides students through the admissions process, coordinating with other organizational units to facilitate enrollment. \u2022 Plans and implements campus and community outreach activities in collaboration with Student Services units and other campus departments. \u2022 Provides policy interpretation and advisement, as appropriate, in accordance with university policies, accreditation standards, and privacy laws. \u2022 Supports the dual credit enrollment process by collaborating with high school partners, students, families, and campus departments to facilitate admissions and application processing. Marketing & Promotion \u2022 Prepares form letters, communications, presentations, and informational and marketing materials in support of recruitment efforts. \u2022 Coordinates inquiry campaigns to engage prospective students and support enrollment initiatives. \u2022 Supports recruitment communications and promotional activities designed to increase awareness of educational opportunities at NMSU-Grants. Data, Application & Enrollment Management \u2022 Manages assigned caseloads of applicants and coordinates admissions inquiries and follow-up activities. \u2022 Processes admissions paperwork (i.e., transcripts) and processing in support of enrollment initiatives. \u2022 Performs miscellaneous job-related duties as assigned. Other Requirements \u2022 Must be available to work occasional evenings and weekends for recruitment events, with corresponding adjustments to the regular work schedule. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 2 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a related field and One (1) year of experience related to the job duties and responsibilities as outlined Special Certification/Licensure: Must be able to obtain an NMSU defensive driving permit. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 25 pounds or standing and/or walking for more than four (4) hours per day. Risk: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c8264b57 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 950850-GRCC STUDENT SERVICES CTR 950850-GRCC STUDENT SERVICES CTR Locations Grants Community College, New Mexico, United States Grants Community College, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 8a043582 Last Name (required) b4eb1d50 Email (required) 882e32f4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 340300-ECONOMICS AND INTERNATIONAL BUSINES The Applied Statistics Program offers MS and PhD degrees in Applied Statistics and a variety of courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The MS program offers courses in both the theory and the application of statistics. The recently launched PhD program is designed to provide graduates with the knowledge of a range of applied statistical methods, both basic and advanced, sufficient to independently solve complex data problems in a collaborative research environment, to teach these methods at the undergraduate level, and to contribute substantively to the development of grant proposals and applied research publications. Facilities Technician Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 470589-FACILITIES MANAGEMENT Join the Facilities Team as a Facilities Tech! Lead Cashier 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Do\u00f1a Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 941210-DACC ACCOUNTING SVCS DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Associate Dean of Students Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Advance a campus culture of accountability, integrity, and student learning at New Mexico State University. We invite applications for an Associate Dean position focused on student conduct adjudication, behavioral accountability, and academic integrity. We seek an experienced leader who brings sound judgment to complex cases, supports fair and consistent processes, and builds strong partnerships with students, faculty, and staff. Join our Student Life team in Las Cruces, New Mexico, and help shape an educational approach to accountability that supports student growth and upholds university standards. Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330020-ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE INSTITUTE New Mexico State University is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning (IAAM). Apply Now First Name (required) 44afd2c9 Last Name (required) 36eb6168 Email (required) 169cafe1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"}, "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-hotel-restaurant-tourism-management-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {"title": "Assistant Professor/Hotel, Restaurant & Tourism Management", "description": "Assistant Professor/Hotel, Restaurant & Tourism Management - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Assistant Professor/Hotel, Restaurant & Tourism Management - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor/Hotel, Restaurant & Tourism Management 504182 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time Closing at: Jan 20 2027 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Elizabeth Stringam, 575-646-7424, betsys@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: If you have the excellence and expertise that will strengthen the university's capacity to engage students, community members, and affiliated researchers on hospitality and tourism issues, apply today! Position Details Position Title: Assistant Professor/Hotel, Restaurant & Tourism Management College/Division: Agricultural,Consumer & Env Sci Col Department: 303600-HOTEL RESTAURANT AND TOURISM MGT Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with the National Education Association (NEA). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The position is 75% teaching, 20% research, 5% service. Success in this position requires excellence and expertise that strengthens the university's capacity to engage students, community members, and affiliated researchers on hospitality and tourism issues. It is envisioned that the faculty member will contribute to enhancing the School's national and international reputation for its undergraduate and graduate programs. Although no formal Extension duties are outlined in the position, outreach and service to stakeholders are an essential aspect of it. Excellence in teaching, both in-person and online formats is required, and includes advising of both undergraduate and graduate students, and assisting with department recruiting and retention efforts. The faculty member is required to perform research, publish and present in peer-reviewed formats, and to solicit financial support for research through grant and industry funding. Service to the profession and on university, college, and departmental committees is also expected. The faculty member will teach three courses per semester. The School of HRTM is part of the College of Agricultural, Consumer and Environmental Sciences, which is home to seven other academic departments, five extension departments, approximately 150 faculty members and 1,800 students. The department offers an undergraduate degree in Hotel, Restaurant and Tourism Management and a graduate Master of Family and Consumer Sciences, HRTM concentration degree and a Graduate Certificate in Hotel, Restaurant and Tourism Management. Both are offered fully online through NMSU Online. HRTM also offers a variety of courses through NMSU On-Demand. For more information about the department, please visit httos://aces.nmsu.edu/academics/shrtm/. ***The following documents are required. Please include on the application: -Your resume/cv -Cover letter -Transcript -Statement of research interests (2-page maximum), and a statement of teaching philosophy and experience (2-page maximum) Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Ph.D. (awarded by hire date) in Hotel, Restaurant, and Tourism Management or related field. The successful candidate will show a commitment to excellence and specific evidence of: (1) interest and expertise in tourism, sustainability, and hospitality and tourism operations; (2) potential to apply research to teaching at both undergraduate and graduate levels; and (3) experience teaching online courses. Demonstrated ability to {1) communicate with various and appropriate audiences (e.g., stakeholders, policymakers, and academics), (2} publish research in appropriate outlets, (3) develop and sustain external funding, and (3) advise both undergraduate and graduate-level students. Demonstrated ability to {1) communicate with various and appropriate audiences (e.g., stakeholders, policymakers, and academic), (2} publish research in appropriate outlets, (3) develop and sustain external funding, and (3) advise both undergraduate and graduate-level students. The department is diverse and multicultural, and the ability to enjoy and thrive in this team-oriented environment will be necessary. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico\u2019s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico\u2019s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives \u2013 and the lives of the people they love \u2013 through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Do\u00f1a Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Do\u00f1a Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated \u201con the hill\u201d above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 5cfece6f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 303600-HOTEL RESTAURANT AND TOURISM MGT 303600-HOTEL RESTAURANT AND TOURISM MGT Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) 5cafd2a3 Last Name (required) 59de6c81 Email (required) 6a7edfa2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Inst